# Supabase Pattern

## Insert example
```typescript
const { data, error } = await supabase
  .from('appointments')
  .insert([appointmentData])
  .select('id')
  .single();

if (error) throw new Error('DB insert failed: ' + error.message);
return data.id;
```

## Migration snippet
```sql
CREATE TABLE appointment_staff (
  appointment_id UUID REFERENCES appointments(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  staff_id UUID REFERENCES staff(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  role TEXT NOT NULL,
  is_primary BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
  google_event_id TEXT,
  PRIMARY KEY (appointment_id, staff_id)
);
```

## Query Patterns
- Always use explicit column selection: `.select('id, name, phone')`
- Check for errors on every response
- Use `.single()` when expecting one result
- Use `.maybeSingle()` when result might not exist
- Always handle RLS policies appropriately

## Error Handling
```typescript
const { data, error } = await supabase.from('table').select('*');
if (error) {
  console.error('Database error:', error);
  throw new Error(`Failed to fetch data: ${error.message}`);
}
```

## UUID Usage
- All primary keys should be UUIDs
- Use `gen_random_uuid()` for new records
- Reference foreign keys with proper constraints
